# Where the pins of deploy/chart/tests/pooler-e2e/ come from, and what each was verified against. `pooler-e2e.sh` reads the `key=value` lines (the comments are
# for people). Almost everything is read from where it is pinned already, so that one pin has one place:
#
#   * the CloudNativePG operator (chart by version and SHA-256), the kind node image and the three tools of the workflow: deploy/chart/tests/backup-e2e/UPSTREAM
#     (`cnpg_chart_*`, `kind_node_image`; the tools are in .github/workflows/pooler-e2e.yml as in backup-e2e.yml);
#   * the pinned `curl` image: deploy/chart/tests/ratelimit-e2e/UPSTREAM (`curl_image`);
#   * the mock issuer's node image: the FROM line of dev/mock-oidc/Dockerfile (tag and digest);
#   * WireMock: the tag compose.yaml pins (`wiremock/wiremock:3.13.2`), and below the digest of that tag, which compose.yaml does not carry.
#
# NOTHING OF THE CLUSTER HALF HAS RUN where this was written (no kind, no container daemon): the first run of the job `pooler-e2e` is the proof or the disproof.
# What was run is `shellcheck`, `dash -n`, `helm template` of every object the script applies, and the orchestrator binary built at the commit that has
# `database.directUrl` (c777d29), whose `--print-config` read the rendered ConfigMap with the two `{ env }` references (deploy/chart/tests/print-config.sh).
#
# VERIFIED 2026-10-28, from the sources named (anonymous requests through the sandbox's proxy; the module sources READ, not run):
#
#   * CloudNativePG 1.30.1 is the operator of backup-e2e/UPSTREAM (chart 0.29.1). Its `Pooler` (api/v1/pooler_types.go at v1.30.1): `spec.cluster.name` (immutable),
#     `spec.type` (`rw`, the default), `spec.instances` (default 1), `spec.template` (a pod template: `spec.containers` is required, and a container named `pgbouncer`
#     is the one whose resources and image are taken), `spec.pgbouncer.poolMode` (`session`, the default, or `transaction`) and `spec.pgbouncer.parameters` (a map of
#     strings). The webhook (internal/webhook/v1/pooler_webhook.go) refuses a parameter that is not in its list; `max_prepared_statements`, `max_client_conn`,
#     `default_pool_size` and `ignore_startup_parameters` are in it, `pool_mode` is not (the mode is the field). A Pooler may not have the name of a Cluster.
#     The Deployment and the Service take the Pooler's name; the Service has the port `pgbouncer` 5432 and the pods a port `metrics` 9127 (pkg/specs/pgbouncer/).
#     PgBouncer is configured with `[databases] * = host=<cluster>-<type>` and authenticates the client's role by `auth_query` as the user `cnpg_pooler_pgbouncer`
#     in the database `postgres` (docs/src/connection_pooling.md, "Authentication"): the role's own password, which the app Secret holds. The configuration is
#     written by the pooler pod's instance manager to /controller/configs/pgbouncer.ini (pkg/management/pgbouncer/config/config.go: ConfigsDir is the scratch directory
#     /controller plus /configs; pkg/postgres/pgconf.go), read there by the script when the pod lets it; the documentation says the operator also keeps a Secret
#     named like the Pooler, whose keys were not looked at. `ignore_startup_parameters` is `extra_float_digits,options` by default.
#   * The default PgBouncer image of 1.30.1 is ghcr.io/cloudnative-pg/pgbouncer:1.25.2 (pkg/versions/versions.go, `DefaultPgbouncerImage`): above the 1.21.0 that
#     `max_prepared_statements` needs (pgbouncer.org/changelog.html). The chart does not set `spec.pgbouncer.image`: the operator's default is the one CloudNativePG
#     tests with. The orchestrator's CI (orchestrator.yml, job `pooler`) ran PgBouncer 1.26.1; 1.22.0 was tried by hand; 1.25.2 is *unverified* with the orchestrator.
#   * The app Secret `<cluster>-app` (pkg/specs/secrets.go at v1.30.1, `CreateSecret`) has these keys and no other: `username`, `user`, `password`, `dbname`, `host`
#     (the `-rw` Service, short name), `port` (5432), `pgpass`, `uri`, `jdbc-uri`, `fqdn-uri`, `fqdn-jdbc-uri`. There is no key for a pooler: `host` is always the
#     cluster's `-rw` Service. The chart builds its two URLs from `username`, `password` and `dbname`.
#   * The password is generated by `password.Generate(64, 10, 0, false, true)` (internal/controller/cluster_create.go, `reconcileAppUserSecret`) of
#     github.com/sethvargo/go-password v0.4.0 (go.mod of v1.30.1): 64 characters, 10 digits, NO symbols, upper case allowed, repeats allowed. The alphabet is then
#     a-z, A-Z and 0-9 (password/generate.go: symbols are added only for numSymbols > 0), which a URL carries without escaping. `uri` is built with `url.UserPassword`
#     (escaped), and the chart does not use it. A password the deployment puts in a Secret of its own (`bootstrap.initdb.secret`, which this chart does not set) is not
#     bound by this: the README says so.
#   * `$(NAME)` in a container's `env` value is expanded by the kubelet from the variables declared above it, including those that come from a `secretKeyRef`
#     (pkg/kubelet/kubelet_pods.go at v1.35.0, `makeEnvironmentVariables`: each resolved value is stored in `tmpEnv` and `expansion.Expand` uses it for the later
#     variables). A reference to a variable that is not defined stays as the text `$(NAME)`; a substituted value is not expanded again.
#   * The pooler's metrics (docs/src/connection_pooling.md, "Monitoring"): `cnpg_pgbouncer_pools_pool_mode{database,user}` (1 session, 2 transaction, 3 statement),
#     `cnpg_pgbouncer_stats_total_xact_count{database}` and `cnpg_pgbouncer_stats_total_client_parse_count{database}`, on port 9127 of each pod.
#   * WireMock 3.13.2: the index digest below, answered by mirror.gcr.io for the tag on 2026-10-28 (Docker Hub answered 429 to the same request).
